## cc-tunnel: when the source is not on this machine

When the `cc-tunnel-workspace` MCP tools (`workspace_*`) are available in a
session, that project's source is on the user's local machine, not here. The
directory this session runs in is a stub that holds rules and memory only.

- Read, search, edit, build, test and run git through the `workspace_*` tools.
  Do not use the built-in file tools or a shell here for project source: they
  see an empty stub and produce answers that look right and are not.
- Call `workspace_status` first. The `cc-tunnel-workspace` skill has the rest.
- If the workspace tools are missing or failing, say so and follow the
  `cc-tunnel-doctor` skill. Never fall back to working on this host.
- After an interruption or a timeout, report a command's result as unknown.
  Do not repeat a side effect, such as a push, migration or deploy, on your own:
  check first whether it already happened.
